Skip meson's threads probe on emscripten.

meson resolves `dependency('threads')` even in emcc cross-builds and appends
`-pthread` to every compile line. clang rejects that when the wasm target is
restricted to MVP features (`-mno-bulk-memory`, `-mno-sign-ext`, ...). We
compile with `-DHB_NO_MT` anyway, so skipping the probe is safe.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -365,7 +365,7 @@ endif

 # threads
 thread_dep = null_dep
-if host_machine.system() != 'windows'
+if host_machine.system() != 'windows' and host_machine.system() != 'emscripten'
   thread_dep = dependency('threads', required: false)

   if thread_dep.found()
